Report #232: "|Hspell:48827|h[Avenger's Shield]|h still 30s cooldown..."
filed at 20:35, five minutes AFTER 0.1.124 went live.

The 0.1.124 fix (clear both the spell entry and the 30s category entry,
then re-arm 6s) ran at +1ms after the cast -- and LOST A RACE. The cast
packet itself hands the client a fresh 30s category entry, and that packet
lands on the client some tens of milliseconds after the cast, i.e. AFTER
the +1ms clear: the client wiped the entry, then immediately re-locked at
30s from the packet, with nothing scheduled to clear it again. Live log at
20:35 showed the server at 6s/category 0 (correct) while the player saw
30s.

Change: two-stage. Stage 1 at +1ms re-arms the server-side flat 6s
(onHold, server pacing true to #132). Stage 2 at +1.5s -- long after the
cast packet has certainly landed, long before the engine's 30s could ever
elapse -- clears the spell entry AND the category entry, then pushes a
fresh 6s cooldown sent to the client, so the icon paces with the server
instead of the engine's 30s. The stale "scheduling deferred 30s clear" log
wording now reads "server re-arm now, client clear at 1.5s".

Touches (module only): modules/mod-living-gear/src/LivingGear_ClassPerks.cpp
(TryPaladinProtOnCast). No core files.
